ValueSet: MII_VS_Mikrobio_LOINC_Ontology_NAA_Detection_Amplification
Id: mii-vs-mikrobio-loinc-ontology-naa-detection-amplification
Title: "MII VS Microbiology LOINC Ontology NAA Detection Amplification"
Description: "Proposal: LOINC codes of the microbiology request 'Specific determination: Nucleic-acid detection — amplification technique asserted', computed by ECL over the LOINC Ontology 2026-10-21. Same, restricted to Technique = << Molecular nucleic acid amplification technique (probe with target amplification, PCR ...). Shows how much a technique clause loses: the generic 'by molecular genetics' and the technique-free codes fall out. Parts: LOINC enumeration (1524, LOINC 2.83), LOINC Ontology observables without LOINC code (0), and the ECL as an intensional include. ECL: `<< 363787002 |Observable entity (observable entity)| : 370130000 |Property (attribute)| = (118589004 |Threshold (property) (qualifier value)| OR 705057003 |Presence (property) (qualifier value)| OR 118584009 |Presence or identity (property) (qualifier value)|), 246093002 |Component (attribute)| = << 117174000 |Nucleic acid sequence with relative specificity for microorganism (substance)|, 246501002 |Technique (attribute)| = << 1156878000 |Molecular nucleic acid amplification technique (qualifier value)|`"
* insert PR_CS_VS_Version
* insert Publisher
* insert SnomedLicense
* ^status = #draft
* ^experimental = true
* ^date = "2026-11-03"
* ^purpose = "Guidance for binding Observation.code of the MII microbiology request profiles to a computably defined LOINC set; accompanies ballot comments on 2027.0.0-ballot2. Generated, not hand-curated."
